{
    "word": "gayness",
    "lang_code": "en",
    "source_file_to_entries": {
        "raw-wiktextract-data.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "186fc113-32a2-3b9d-81f4-b09267fd2bf8",
                "word": "gayness",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "c5cc99bc-322e-4e55-a936-ef782c6bdeb1",
                        "entry_id": "186fc113-32a2-3b9d-81f4-b09267fd2bf8",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "gaynesses"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "4592b5c7-a536-39ee-a9f5-41d824a3e34d",
                        "entry_id": "186fc113-32a2-3b9d-81f4-b09267fd2bf8",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The state of being gay (colorful or festive); display or dressiness."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "dated",
                            "rare",
                            "uncountable",
                            "usually"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "a350480e-dc89-4eda-a970-6163c3bf11db",
                                "sense_id": "4592b5c7-a536-39ee-a9f5-41d824a3e34d",
                                "text": "And truly, at a short butt, which some men doth use, the peacock feather doth seldom keep up the shaft either right or level, it is so rough and heavy ; so that many men, which have taken them up for gayness, hath laid them down again for profit:"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b98c16bd-3efa-4eab-9f37-7ed264064f6f",
                                "sense_id": "4592b5c7-a536-39ee-a9f5-41d824a3e34d",
                                "text": "Let me ſpeak prowdly: Tell the Conſtable, ⁠/ We are but Warriors for the working-day: / Our Gayneſſe and our Gilt are all beſmyrcht / With raynie Marching in the painefull field."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "bed89550-f6a1-3ff3-adf5-0ae2f48a0c6e",
                        "entry_id": "186fc113-32a2-3b9d-81f4-b09267fd2bf8",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The state of being gay (cheerful); gaiety."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "countable",
                            "dated",
                            "rare",
                            "usually"
                        ],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "43a27be5-130b-3a24-bfc2-40899308afab",
                        "entry_id": "186fc113-32a2-3b9d-81f4-b09267fd2bf8",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The state of being gay (homosexual); homosexuality; demeanor stereotypically representative of it."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "uncountable",
                            "usually"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "121b9626-aa6e-41ab-b242-e849678cbb07",
                                "sense_id": "43a27be5-130b-3a24-bfc2-40899308afab",
                                "text": "You cannot blame their gayness, their queerness, their homosexuality on sudden wealth."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ea9da0be-c9b7-4dc1-861f-4c9fd84c8c89",
                                "sense_id": "43a27be5-130b-3a24-bfc2-40899308afab",
                                "text": "Tell Al Sublette I met a great new pianist called Cecil Taylor, [he] plays like [Oscar] Peterson gone Classical, fast runs but Brubeck-Stravinsky-Prokofieff chords, a Juilliard classicist—He, like [James] Baldwin, [is] colored, [and] I think gay,—Baldwin is gay. I don’t dig all this gayness."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "1d45d171-3cef-40a3-89cc-4bd8679e008b",
                                "sense_id": "43a27be5-130b-3a24-bfc2-40899308afab",
                                "text": "I doubt very much that their \"gay­ness\" had any deep sexual roots. I think it was simply an exotic form of juvenile delinquency."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "66e454ec-ff62-4f61-accc-f0ab7dd883ab",
                                "sense_id": "43a27be5-130b-3a24-bfc2-40899308afab",
                                "text": "Those of us who have been in heterosexual marriages too often have blamed our gayness on the breakup of the marriage."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "30f28ce5-5211-47fe-9664-cc2de4c58c50",
                                "sense_id": "43a27be5-130b-3a24-bfc2-40899308afab",
                                "text": "Were there gay people in the ancient world, or is gayness a uniquely modern category?"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "8a4598fa-9393-401c-b138-656794205218",
                                "sense_id": "43a27be5-130b-3a24-bfc2-40899308afab",
                                "text": "Their goal was to compel open legal recognition of their beliefs about sex and gayness as being the law in the United States."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "63878761-14df-4a19-b781-34d90a0f984f",
                        "source_entry_id": "186fc113-32a2-3b9d-81f4-b09267fd2bf8",
                        "source_sense_description": "the state of being cheerful",
